  "slug": "cellular-electron-economy-e434",
  "summary": "A new preprint cuts B-factor factorization cost from O(N^3) to O(Nk^3), while published ML work targets other properties, with fixed-solvent splits and fast spectroscopy surrogates.",
  "synthesis": "The one item that bears directly on reduced protein dynamics is a preprint introducing a local magnitude representation for B-factor prediction from C-alpha structure, lowering factorization cost from O(N^3) to O(Nk^3). Its emphasis is on a compact, structure-derived description of fluctuations that avoids dense global computation. The remaining items are published machine-learning studies on other tasks: fungal peroxygenase substrate prediction, solubility prediction for unseen solvents with QM-derived σ-moment descriptors, Mössbauer parameter prediction matching DFT accuracy at 218-fold lower cost, and geometry-aware retention time index approximation. These share a surrogate-for-costly-computation motif but address different observables and are not a common benchmark. Support for a unified dynamics-reduction thread is therefore limited to the B-factor work.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-10"
}
